Charlie: They say if you move fast enough, nothing sticks.
Charlie: I've been practicing. I know exactly where to step, and definitely where not to.
Charlie: From gutters. From hands. From mistakes.
Charlie: But no matter how far I go, some things still catch my eye.
Charlie: And tonight, I’m running.
Charlie: Not to disappear, but to gather everything I need to make it back.
